Repository: {{repo_full}} at commit {{commit_sha}}.
Program URL: {{extra.bug_bounty_url}}
Rules checked at: {{extra.program_rules_checked_at}}
Program snapshot: {{extra.program_rules_snapshot}}
Deployment evidence: {{extra.deployment_evidence}}
Known-issues snapshot: {{extra.known_issues_snapshot}}
Authorized testing constraints: {{extra.authorized_test_constraints}}

Build the immutable scope contract for this run before analyzing code. Extract exact in-scope assets/components, accepted impacts, exclusions, known issues, testing restrictions, payout priorities, and supplied deployment facts. Separate supplied evidence from missing facts. Never infer current program rules, live deployments, TVL, traffic, configuration, or severity from memory. A silent snapshot creates a scope gap.

Return exactly one record. Preserve the wording or a close identifier for each controlling rule so later agents can map a technical effect to a named accepted impact. Do not analyze vulnerabilities.

Extract exact tokenomics assets/contracts/addresses/chains, accepted theft/freeze/governance impacts, cross-chain and trusted-relayer rules, impact thresholds, and deployment snapshot. Do not exclude bridges, gauges, or audited modules unless the supplied scope controls.

Independently analyze {{surface_operation_label}}. Hunt vote-weight bias/slope forgery, checkpoint omission/reordering, week/epoch boundary double counting, emission over-allocation, stale gauge state, flash/composable voting where feasible, rounding accumulation, and cross-module/cross-chain message replay allowed by scope. Require a concrete value or governance impact path, exact math/state drift, realistic prerequisites, guards, and falsification target.

Use the mapped neighborhood, not only the focal operation:
- proxy/initialization: {{surface_proxy_and_initialization_trace}}
- storage risks: {{surface_storage_layout_risks}}
- call edges: {{surface_cross_contract_edges}}
- related public operations: {{surface_related_operations}}
- shared state: {{surface_shared_state_dependencies}}

Explicitly test cross-contract sequences of two or more public operations when they share accounting, authorization, oracle, callback, approval, epoch, or settlement state. Include sequences where one operation creates a state that another consumes in the same transaction, later transaction, callback, or flash-loan bundle.

Explicit proxy/storage classes: uninitialized proxy or implementation; initializer/reinitializer replay; implementation takeover with a concrete effect on the proxy or assets; UUPS/transparent/beacon/diamond upgrade authorization bypass; storage-layout collision across evidenced versions; facet/selector clashing; delegatecall to an attacker-controlled or incorrectly validated target; proxy/implementation authorization disagreement; immutable/domain-separator/address-context mistakes under delegatecall; and upgrade paths that brick, seize, mint, withdraw, or permanently freeze in-scope value. Emit a hypothesis only with an evidenced deployed path, attacker-controlled primitive, exact faulty slot/selector/initializer/authorization operation, and accepted-impact candidate.

Create one report only for an eligible candidate with technical_verdict=supported and poc_verdict reproduced or deterministically_proven. Re-read every cited source location. Point file_path and line to the faulty operation or missing protection. Explain the attacker-controlled production path, the failed invariant, why every material guard fails, the observed impact, and the exact program mapping. Distinguish repository facts, supplied runtime facts, reproduction evidence, and remaining assumptions.

trigger_flow must be an ordered attacker-to-impact trace. malicious_input_example must be the smallest safe representation of the exploit condition for an authorized isolated target or local fork. Set exploitable=true only when the stated actor can complete the chain under the evidenced production configuration. Preserve root_bug_fingerprint, verdicts, asset, impact, severity, confidence, assumptions, and artifact references from the ranked record.

